  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency WASH and nutrition (preventative and curative) services for drought-affected children and families</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $3 million UNICEF project is to provide drought-affected people with life-saving support in the Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) and Nutrition clusters. In terms of WASH support, UNICEF will provide 45-60 days of emergency water trucking and distribute 10,000 emergency hygiene kits, construct 300 latrines for internally displaced people and rehabilitate 10 strategic waterpoints, among other activities, reaching a total of 60,000 people, including 18,570 women, 23,509 children and 9,000 people with disabilities. In terms of Nutrition support, UNICEF will feed 79,210 children with high energy biscuits and 36,000 children with therapeutic milk and implement information sessions on optimal feeding techniques, among other activities.  In total, the Nutrition component will reach 250,210 people, including 135,000 women,  115,210 children, and 17,450 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
